NEARS-1628 QA — pre-existing DATA gap: two wallet surfaces are untestable
Found: 2026-08-09. NOT caused by this ticket's diff. Read-only queries only.

1) The wallet bonus banner can never render in any QA run.
   mysql> SELECT COUNT(*) FROM wallet_bonuses;        -> 0
   Backend: WalletController@get_bonus does
       WalletBonus::Active()->Running()->latest()->get()
   so the endpoint returns [] for every user.
   UserApp bonus_banner_widget.dart:20-21 gates on
       fundBonusList != null && fundBonusList!.isNotEmpty
   Live isolate on the success path (Dart VM service evaluate):
       Get.find<WalletController>().fundBonusList!.length  -> 0
   => "the bonus banner populates" is unreachable by construction.

2) Wallet pagination / load-more can never fire.
   mysql> SELECT COUNT(*) FROM wallet_transactions;   -> 6   (whole DB)
   mysql> SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) FROM wallet_transactions GROUP BY user_id;
          user_id 3 -> 4      user_id 1 -> 2
   Request observed: GET /api/v1/customer/wallet/transactions?offset=1&limit=10
   Live isolate: Get.find<WalletController>().canLoadMore -> false
   => the scroll listener's load-more branch (wallet_screen.dart:96-113) is
      unreachable; no seeded user has more than one page.

Impact: every wallet ticket inherits two permanently undemonstrable ACs.
Needs a versioned, identity-guarded seeder (>=1 Active+Running wallet_bonuses
row, and >=11 wallet_transactions rows for one test user). QA cannot seed it
(read-only DB rule).
